  "text": "Neither solution gives the correct constant, so the answer is NONE.\n\nThe bound must refine $n \\le 2m-3$ for every $k \\ge 3$, so at $k=3$ it cannot exceed $2m-3$. That requires $\\lfloor (3+c)/2 \\rfloor \\ge 3$, i.e. $c \\ge 3$.\n\n- **Solution 1 ($c=1$):** At $k=3$ the bound is $2m-\\lfloor 4/2\\rfloor = 2m-2$, which is weaker than $2m-3$. It is not a refinement. Its reasoning is also a guess about parity, not a derivation.\n- **Solution 2 ($c=2$):** At $k=3$ the bound is $2m-\\lfloor 5/2\\rfloor = 2m-2$, again weaker than $2m-3$. The solution itself notices this, then asserts $c=2$ anyway by appeal to an unnamed \"source,\" which is not a valid justification.\n\nThe consistent value is $c \\ge 3$. I believe the source result is $c=3$, which reproduces $2m-3$ exactly at $k=3$ and tightens for larger $k$, but I have not verified this against the paper. Either way, neither listed answer satisfies the stated refinement condition.\n\nCHOICE: NONE",
